WEBVTT

00:06.160 --> 00:09.360
Education and training can help you feel more confident

00:09.360 --> 00:13.120
and enable you to achieve successful catheterization.

00:13.120 --> 00:15.680
You can use this step-by-step video as support

00:15.680 --> 00:18.440
and follow up on any training provided.

00:18.440 --> 00:20.640
Always follow the advice and instructions

00:20.800 --> 00:22.680
provided by a clinician which are tailored

00:22.680 --> 00:27.000
to your individual medical and lifestyle needs.

00:27.000 --> 00:30.040
So what is intermittent catheterization?

00:30.040 --> 00:33.760
Intermittent catheterization helps empty your bladder when

00:33.760 --> 00:36.000
your body can't do it on its own.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.440
It involves emptying your bladder regularly

00:38.680 --> 00:42.600
with a hollow tube with drainage holes, a catheter.

00:42.600 --> 00:45.000
The catheter is inserted in your urethra,

00:45.000 --> 00:47.680
which is the tube between the bladder and the exit,

00:47.680 --> 00:53.720
allowing the urine to flow down the catheter and out.

00:53.720 --> 00:56.200
Let's briefly go through the body parts

00:56.200 --> 00:59.280
involved in the urinary system.

00:59.280 --> 00:59.920
Kidney.

00:59.920 --> 01:03.360
Your kidneys are two small bean shaped organs

01:03.360 --> 01:06.080
that clean your blood and make urine.

01:06.080 --> 01:07.120
Ureter.

01:07.520 --> 01:09.320
The ureters are thin tubes

01:09.320 --> 01:13.160
that carry urine from the kidneys down to the bladder.

01:13.160 --> 01:13.680
Bladder.

01:14.560 --> 01:17.480
The bladder is a hollow stretchy organ in your

01:17.480 --> 01:19.880
lower belly that stores urine.

01:19.880 --> 01:21.480
Urethra.

01:21.480 --> 01:23.320
The urethra is the tube

01:23.320 --> 01:26.840
that carries urine from the bladder out of the body.

01:26.840 --> 01:31.440
And finally, the urethral opening.

01:31.440 --> 01:34.160
It is quite usual to feel a little anxious

01:34.160 --> 01:37.480
or worried when starting something new for the first time.

01:37.480 --> 01:39.200
But with practice and support,

01:39.200 --> 01:41.040
you will soon become more confident

01:41.120 --> 01:43.040
with intermittent catheterization

01:43.040 --> 01:45.200
and it will soon become a natural part

01:45.200 --> 01:46.320
of your daily routine.

01:47.360 --> 01:52.520
Now let's talk through how to use LoFric Elle Pro step-by-step.

01:52.520 --> 01:56.440
Start by washing your hands thoroughly with soap and water.

01:56.440 --> 01:58.520
You can also use cleansing wipes

01:58.520 --> 02:01.280
if you don't have access to running water.

02:01.280 --> 02:04.720
Cleanse your hands again after catheterization.

02:04.720 --> 02:05.720
Open the upper lid.

02:06.360 --> 02:08.040
Hold the catheter in one hand

02:08.240 --> 02:11.080
and gently bend the upper part to open.

02:11.080 --> 02:13.040
Pull the catheter out.

02:13.040 --> 02:16.440
Connect the container to the catheter with a gentle twist,

02:16.440 --> 02:20.400
making sure the arrow on the container points down.

02:20.400 --> 02:23.320
LoFric Elle Pro is an intermittent catheter

02:23.320 --> 02:25.040
with a unique L-shaped handle

02:25.040 --> 02:28.080
that helps you confidently locate the urethra.

02:28.080 --> 02:31.280
Sitting on the toilet is ideal for doing IC,

02:31.280 --> 02:32.440
but if not possible,

02:32.760 --> 02:34.880
your clinician will help you find a position

02:34.880 --> 02:36.880
that suits you best.

02:36.880 --> 02:40.480
Tilt your pelvis upwards and spread your labia.

02:40.480 --> 02:43.840
Hold the handle with your dominant hand gently

02:43.840 --> 02:48.160
and slowly guide the catheter into the urethra.

02:48.160 --> 02:51.440
The urethral entrance is small and sometimes hard to see.

02:51.440 --> 02:52.840
And using a mirror can help.

02:53.560 --> 02:57.240
It is just above the vaginal opening and below the clitoris.

02:57.240 --> 02:58.600
It is close to the anus.

02:58.920 --> 03:02.640
So keeping clean is important to prevent infection.

03:02.640 --> 03:04.520
Once urine starts to flow,

03:04.520 --> 03:07.520
the catheter is in the right place.

03:07.520 --> 03:09.400
Gently insert a little further

03:09.400 --> 03:11.120
to ensure it's fully in your bladder.

03:11.840 --> 03:14.120
Wait until urine flow stops.

03:14.120 --> 03:18.000
LoFric Elle Pro allows for complete bladder emptying.

03:18.000 --> 03:19.720
Now slowly withdraw the catheter.

03:20.480 --> 03:23.040
The unique LoFric surface coating will ensure

03:23.040 --> 03:26.320
that the catheter remains smoothly lubricated.

03:26.320 --> 03:29.520
Put the catheter back inside the container.

03:29.520 --> 03:32.480
Remember, LoFric Elle Pro is a urinary catheter designed

03:32.480 --> 03:35.120
to be used one time only.

03:35.120 --> 03:38.200
Dispose or carry it in your bag until disposal.

03:38.200 --> 03:43.160
Please note the lower container is recyclable.

03:43.160 --> 03:46.440
How often you catheterize will vary individually

03:46.440 --> 03:49.000
and also depend upon fluid intake.

03:49.000 --> 03:50.720
Your clinician will advise you

03:50.720 --> 03:53.040
on the right regime for you.

03:53.040 --> 03:56.120
LoFric Elle Pro is your versatile single use

03:56.120 --> 03:59.480
intermittent catheter ready for you,

03:59.480 --> 04:01.000
whatever your lifestyle needs.
